# Welcome!

This professional learning module is designed to prepare you to teach Code.org’s Thinking Critically About AI unit, part of the AI Discoveries curriculum. This unit invites students to explore artificial intelligence not just as users, but as thoughtful evaluators, testers, and decision-makers. 

Through hands-on investigations, discussions, and project work, students examine how AI systems generate outputs, where those systems succeed or fail, and what role humans should play when using AI responsibly. Throughout the unit, students build a “Generate and Judge” guide that captures their evidence, reflections, and recommendations for responsible AI use.

___


