<hr aria-hidden="true">


By the end of this professional learning module, you will be able to:

* Explain how the unit helps students develop critical thinking habits around AI systems.
* Guide students in evaluating AI outputs for accuracy, bias, privacy and safety risks, credibility, and appropriateness.
* Facilitate classroom discussions that move students beyond binary thinking (“AI is good” or “AI is bad”).
* Support students in collecting evidence, identifying patterns in AI behavior, and using those findings to build claims and recommendations.
* Understand how the unit project develops and supports authentic student voice, inquiry, critique, and reflection.

